<NAME>FPIF private markets target</NAME>
<CONTENT>In FPIF’s February 13, 2023 RFP for Private Markets Investment Consulting and Discretionary OCIO Advisory Services, FPIF says it is constructing a long-term target allocation of 31% to private market asset classes.

The target split is:
- Private equity: 10%
- Private debt: 7%
- Real estate: 10%
- Infrastructure: 4%

The RFP also adds that, within the real estate and infrastructure target allocations, 50% is intended for core open-ended vehicles, with the remaining 50% intended for non-core commitments.</CONTENT>
