[role=assistant] <DESCRIPTION>The relevant evidence indicates the TRS minimum qualification is found in Appendix B of the investment consulting services RFP. A firm must certify a client-experience threshold tied to institutional pension fund relationships, not a separate $10 billion private equity client-assets requirement in the provided TRS document.</DESCRIPTION>
<NAME>TRS minimum certification</NAME>
<CONTENT>In the provided Teachers’ Retirement System of the State of Illinois (TRS) RFP evidence, the minimum qualification a firm must certify is:

- **As of December 31, 2022, it has at least five (5) institutional pension fund clients.**

Appendix B, “Statement of Minimum Qualifications,” also requires the firm to certify that:

1. **It is currently providing investment consulting services to clients whose combined assets total at least $50 billion.**
2. **The primary consultant proposed for the TRS account has at least five (5) years of experience providing domestic and international investment consulting services to public and/or private pension funds.**
3. **As of December 31, 2022, it has at least five (5) institutional pension fund clients.**

So, based on the TRS evidence provided, the minimum client experience certification is **at least five institutional pension fund clients**. There is **no support in the provided TRS document** for a separate requirement that the firm certify private equity consulting experience for clients with at least $10 billion in private equity assets.</CONTENT>
