[role=assistant] <DESCRIPTION>The IMRF sample RFP for domestic equity small cap growth investment management states that respondents are evaluated and ranked during the selection process on four primary factors. These factors are people, process, performance, and pricing.</DESCRIPTION>
<NAME>IMRF ranking factors</NAME>
<CONTENT>In the IMRF sample RFP for domestic equity small cap growth investment management, all respondents are evaluated and ranked on four primary factors during the selection process:

1. **People** — the **stability of the organization**, **ownership structure**, and **documented experience of key professionals**.

2. **Process** — whether the firm has a **clearly defined, reasonable, and repeatable investment strategy**.

3. **Performance** — the firm’s **documented ability to meet investment performance benchmarks**.

4. **Pricing** — the **fee schedule and associated costs**.

The RFP states this in Part 8, Section 8.1, under the selection process.</CONTENT>
