<NAME>BCERS 7-year minimum.</NAME>
<CONTENT>In the Baltimore City Employees’ Retirement Systems (BCERS) RFP for an Alternatives Consultant, the proposing firm must have been in business for **at least seven (7) years**.

The relevant language appears in Section I.E, “Minimum Qualifications,” which states that:

- **“The firm must have been in business for at least seven (7) or more years providing general consulting services plus private equity consulting services or alternatives consulting services only.”**

This is listed as a mandatory minimum qualification, and the RFP further notes that failure to satisfy each minimum qualification may result in immediate rejection of the proposal. It also says that all minimum qualifications must be met as of **November 8, 2024, 3:00 P.M. EDT**.</CONTENT>
