[role=assistant] <DESCRIPTION>The Monroe County 457(b) deferred compensation RFP, which is subject to New York State Deferred Compensation Board rules and the State Model Plan, states both the Model Plan minimum annual deferral and the deadline for investing participant deferrals. The relevant provisions appear in Section I under “Specifications of the Model Plan.”</DESCRIPTION>
<NAME>Model Plan minimums.</NAME>
<CONTENT>The minimum deferral amount required by the Model Plan is <b>$260 for any plan year</b>. This is stated in Section I, “Specifications of the Model Plan,” subsection 1, which cites <b>Section 3.2(a)</b>: “The Model Plan requires a minimum deferral amount to be $260 for any plan year.”

Participant deferrals must be invested <b>no later than two (2) business days following receipt</b>. This appears in the same section under subsection 2, citing <b>Section 4.1</b>: amounts deferred by participants “will be invested, according to the participant’s investment directions, no later than two (2) business days following receipt thereof, in the appropriate investment funds.”

So the answer is:
- <b>Minimum deferral:</b> $260 per plan year
- <b>Investment deadline:</b> within 2 business days after receipt</CONTENT>
