<NAME>NJEDA ESG Questions</NAME>
<CONTENT>Under section 10.0 “ESG (Environmental, Social, Governance)” of the NJEDA Life Science Seed Fund due diligence questionnaire (Appendix A), the following questions are asked:

1. **10.1.** Describe the role of respondent’s internal advisory board(s). Detail all matters referred to the advisory board(s), including any currently unresolved matters. Describe any additional governing/advisory bodies that impact the management or investment activity of respondent (e.g. CEO Circle, operating committee, management affiliate, etc.).

2. **10.2.** Detail any conflicts of interest (potential, current and historic) within respondent, and explain how they have been/are identified, managed, disclosed (to Limited Partner Advisory Committee (LPAC) or otherwise) and resolved. Identify any committees in place to help with the resolution of conflicts (conflict committee, etc.).

3. **10.3.** What is respondent’s policy of personal investments by any employees or affiliates in deals reviewed by the respondent (both accepted and rejected)? If applicable, provide a list of all previous investments of this nature.

4. **10.4.** Is respondent a registered investment advisor (RIA)?

5. **10.5.** What are respondent’s ESG-related policies and how do ESG factors influence respondent’s investment beliefs?

6. **10.6.** What is the current implementation status of respondent’s responsible investment policy? Does respondent have any firm plans to develop respondent’s approach towards the management of ESG factors?

7. **10.7.** How does respondent contribute to portfolio companies’ management of ESG-related risks and opportunities?

8. **10.8.** What monitoring processes would respondent have in place to assess the proposed Fund’s portfolio companies’ management of ESG factors?

Note: although labeled as “ESG,” this section also includes governance-focused questions on advisory boards, conflicts of interest, personal investment policy, and RIA status, followed by ESG-policy and monitoring questions.</CONTENT>
