<NAME>SBCERS assets figure.</NAME>
<CONTENT>As of September 30, 2023, the Santa Barbara County Employees' Retirement System (SBCERS) had total assets of $4,112,337,498.26 according to the SBCERS Global Custody and Related Services RFP Addendum I dated January 8, 2024.

The RFP’s “Accounts and Assets at September 30, 2023” table also indicates:
- Total accounts: 33
- Total assets: $4,112,337,498.26
- Total non-cash line item holdings: 224

The asset breakdown listed in the addendum is:
- Cash accounts: $57,223,039.65
- Domestic separate accounts: $708,161,794.76
- Global separate accounts: $341,676,532.73
- Single line commingled funds: $1,496,774,362.02
- Multi line commingled funds: $1,502,851,575.98
- Residuals accounts: $5,650,193.12

In short, SBCERS had about $4.112 billion in assets as of September 30, 2023.</CONTENT>
