[role=assistant] <DESCRIPTION>The PRS-STL actuarial auditing services RFP states a minimum experience requirement for the principal actuary. It requires the principal actuary assigned to PRS-STL to have at least five years of professional actuarial experience.</DESCRIPTION>
<NAME>Principal actuary: 5 years.</NAME>
<CONTENT>In the Police Retirement System of St. Louis (PRS-STL) actuarial RFP, the principal actuary assigned to provide services to PRS-STL must have a minimum of five (5) years of professional actuarial experience.

The relevant section appears under “Mandatory Minimum Qualifications,” which specifies that the principal actuary must:
- have a minimum of five (5) years professional actuarial experience,
- be an enrolled actuary,
- be a Member of the American Academy of Actuaries,
- and be an Associate of the Society of Actuaries, with Fellowship preferred.

The RFP also separately requires that the principal actuary have a minimum of five (5) years of experience testifying before legislative and administrative bodies in support of actuarial positions and/or valuation principles.</CONTENT>
[role=assistant] <SUMMARY>
# Briefing

## Answer
The **principal actuary must have a minimum of five (5) years of professional actuarial experience**.

## Supporting Context
Under **Mandatory Minimum Qualifications**, the PRS-STL actuarial RFP states that the principal actuary must also:
- be an **enrolled actuary**,
- be a **Member of the American Academy of Actuaries**,
- be an **Associate of the Society of Actuaries** (**Fellowship preferred**).

## Additional Note
The RFP separately requires the principal actuary to have **five (5) years of experience testifying** before legislative and administrative bodies in support of actuarial positions and/or valuation principles.
</SUMMARY>
